# Study results (participant data - never commit)
#
# This now covers Logs/audio/, which holds one WAV per utterance: a participant's
# recorded voice, which is personal data and identifying in a way the CSVs are
# not. The rule already matched it, but it is worth saying out loud — a stray
# `git add -f Logs` would publish recordings of named people to a public fork.
Logs/

# Demo and session footage. Never commit: clips show a real person's face and
# voice, which is personal data no consent form here covers for redistribution.
Recordings/
*.slnx

# Generated Word copies of the markdown documents. Rebuild with:
#   node Server/scripts/md2docx.js STUDY_DESIGN.md          docs/Say-It-Again-Study-Design.docx
#   node Server/scripts/md2docx.js docs/SUPERVISOR_BRIEF.md docs/Say-It-Again-Supervisor-Brief.docx
#   node Server/scripts/md2docx.js docs/PREREGISTRATION.md  docs/Say-It-Again-Preregistration.docx
#   node Server/scripts/md2docx.js docs/RELATED_WORK.md    docs/Say-It-Again-Related-Work.docx
docs/Say-It-Again-Related-Work.docx
#
# Not committed for the same reason the poster is not: a build product that can
# drift from its source is worse than no build product, because whoever opens it
# has no way to tell which version of the design they are reading.
docs/Say-It-Again-Study-Design.docx
docs/Say-It-Again-Supervisor-Brief.docx
docs/Say-It-Again-Preregistration.docx

# Generated poster artefacts — rebuild with Server/scripts/build-poster.sh
study-poster.pdf
study-qr.svg
study-qr.png
study-site/poster-print.html
study-site/poster-built.html
# Same three artefacts for the other two studies, whose sources live in
# study-site/omni-connect/ and study-site/indoor-room/. Covered already by the
# study-site/ rule below, listed here so the pattern is not a surprise.
Unity/OldAgentVoice_unused/

# Participant landing page — separate repo, pushed to abyyworld/vr-voice-study
study-site/

# Unity crash dumps. Written next to the project when the editor dies, and one
# of them is thousands of lines of stack trace that briefly got committed by an
# over-eager sync.
mono_crash.*.json
**/mono_crash.*.json
